Bootstrap: docker
From: ubuntu:20.04

# ============================================================================
# net.def — apptainer/singularity container for netMHCstabpan-1.0
# Service: quantimmu-bench §tools_present  lever=netMHCstabpan-1.0 (MHC-peptide
#          stability, DTU tool)
#
# WHY A CONTAINER (root cause, do NOT re-debug):
#   The netMHCstabpan-1.0 binary (and its netMHCpan-2.8 backend) is linked
#   against GLIBC_2.29. The HPC login/compute nodes run el8 with glibc 2.28,
#   so running the binary directly fails with:
#       ./netMHCpan: version `GLIBC_2.29' not found
#   ubuntu:20.04 ships glibc 2.31 → satisfies GLIBC_2.29 at RUNTIME.
#
#   Rejected alternatives (researcher 2026-06-29):
#     - conda sysroot / cross-glibc: fixes COMPILE time, NOT runtime → no good.
#     - patchelf --set-interpreter: extremely brittle on a closed-source DTU
#       binary that also dlopen's helpers → rejected.
#   Container = the path LENS (uselens.io) officially uses to ship the DTU
#   net* trio. Proven precedent.
#
# WHAT GOES IN THE CONTAINER vs WHAT IS BIND-MOUNTED:
#   In container : only the runtime (glibc 2.31) + tcsh + gawk (the wrapper
#                  scripts are tcsh and use gawk).
#   Bind-mounted : the ext_tools tree (netMHCstabpan-1.0 + netMHCpan-2.8
#                  backend + their data dirs) — see run_netmhcstabpan.sh.
#   We do NOT copy the DTU binaries into the image (academic license + size).
#
# BUILD — two routes (pick by whether HPC has fakeroot/user-namespaces):
#   Route 1 (HPC has fakeroot enabled):
#       apptainer build --fakeroot net.sif net.def
#   Route 2 (no fakeroot on HPC):
#       # build where you have root (local Linux box / WSL2 / a VM):
#       sudo apptainer build net.sif net.def        # or singularity build
#       # then copy the .sif up to HPC:
#       scp net.sif jiayu2403@<hpc>:/gpfs/work/bio/jiayu2403/quantimmu/HPC/deploy/netmhcstabpan/
#   ⚠️ scp of net.sif to HPC = outbound transfer = MAIN-THREAD decision point
#      (this kit does NOT upload anything).
# ============================================================================

%post
    apt-get update && apt-get install -y tcsh gawk wget vim
    apt-get clean && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

%labels
    Tool netMHCstabpan-1.0
    Service quantimmu-bench
    Purpose MHC-peptide stability scoring (DTU), glibc-2.29 runtime shim

%help
    Runtime container for netMHCstabpan-1.0. Bind ext_tools in, run the
    DTU binary through `apptainer exec`. See run_netmhcstabpan.sh and README.md
    for the bind layout and the tcsh-wrapper NMHOME/TMPDIR rewrite checklist.
